Z||000000||Taijiguy||03-28-2001||02:01 PM||||Been on a search for sail panels. I picked up a set from my favorite u-pull-it yard today. The ones I got are different from the ones I had. The old ones, the panel mounted to the frame from behind. These new ones, the panel mounts to the front of the frame. Any commentary on these?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||03-28-2001||02:12 PM||||Are these notchback or GT sail panels?<P>What year car do you have and what year did you pull your new ones from?<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||5
Z||000002||Taijiguy||03-28-2001||02:19 PM||||These are notchback panels. The originals (with the filler mounted from behind) came from my '85. And I *think* the original was actully glass. The ones I just picked up, I have no idea the year, but I'm sure is at least an 85 or 86. The filler is mountd from the outside with tape, and is definetly plexiglass.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||03-28-2001||03:00 PM||||84 notchbacks were the only year that had glass panels. the 85-88 were all plexi. if you had glass on your 85, someone switched them out with an 84. on my 86 sc, one of them is glass, one is plexi, but i have a new glass. just need to put it on there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>hope this helps.<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.JPG">  <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||03-28-2001||03:13 PM||||1984 = glass<BR>1985 thru 88 = plastic<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||Taijiguy||03-28-2001||03:17 PM||||Well, I bought these plastic ones, but I think I'll keep looking for a right side glass one. I like the glass better.||||reg||1
